      "translation": "The ocean appears blue due to the way water interacts with sunlight. Sunlight is composed of all colors of the rainbow, but water molecules preferentially absorb the longer wavelengths, such as red, orange, and yellow. This absorption leaves the shorter, high-energy wavelengths, like blue and violet, to scatter in all directions. This phenomenon is called Rayleigh scattering. When we look at the ocean, our eyes detect this scattered blue light, making the vast expanse of water appear blue. The clarity of the water also influences the intensity of the blue hue.",
